speechtext:
With regard to boards of arbitration and conciliation under the Industrial Disputes Act, I have received a long resolution, passed by System Federation No. 11 of the Intercolonial and Prince Edward Island Railways, complaining that the Grand Trunk Pacific Railway officials will not recognize the decision of the arbitration board in regard to difficulties between the railway , and the employees.
I will read the resolution; it is as follows:
Whereas the workers are from time to time urged and are expected to live up to the spirit of conciliation and arbitration and award ot the board appointed under the Industrial Disputes Act;

And whereas we expect as workers that in accepting that spirit of the law, the employers should accept it in the same spirit, and when agreeing to the creation of such a board, they should accept such a decision;
And whereas the Grand Trunk Pacific railway, in view of certain considerations guaranteed by the Dominion Government, agreed to accept and be bound by an award of a board appointed to consider the condition of workers ( on that road;
And whereas up to the present time the management of the Grand Trunk Pacific railway have refused to put into operation the award of the said board, and such refusal being a serious violation of the spirit and intent of the Industrial Disputes Act:
And whereas many millions of the public money have been spent by the Grand Trunk Pacific railway, and as said company has frequently received valuable concessions from the Dominion Government, and therefore they should be compelled to respect the Industrial Disputes Act:
Therefore, be it resolved that this System Federation of the Canadian Government railways co-operate with the workers on other railroads in Canada and the Trades and Dabour Congress in entering our protest against the Dominion Government granting any more ac-sistance to the said railroad until such a time as they live up to the award of the late Board of Arbitration dealing with the conditions of the employees on said road.
Has the minister taken any action in this matter?
